course: dictionary
lesson: 10179
title: Tighten: firmer, tighter, stricter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tighten means to make something tighter or firmer. You tighten a screw, or your shoelaces, so they hold well. The clues are in the word around it: a screw or a lace is something that can be pulled firm.
explain: It can also mean to become tighter, with no one doing the pulling. «His grip tightened.» Nobody tightened his hand. The sentence tells us his hand squeezed harder, so grip is the clue that it is about holding.
explain: Tighten can mean making rules stricter, too. «The school tightened the rules.» A rule cannot be pulled like a shoelace, so ask: what would fit here? Stricter fits, and it makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Some phrases use tighten in a special way. «Tighten your belt» means spend less money, not pull a belt tight. When a phrase seems odd, read the whole sentence first, then check your meaning.
fact: Tighten is a verb: tighten, tightens, tightened, tightening.
fact: «Tighten» means to make something tighter or firmer, to become tighter, or to make rules stricter.
fact: «Tighten your belt» means spend less money. «Tighten up» and «tighten your grip» are other phrases to know.
fact: «We fixin' to tighten belts» is from Atlanta: «fixin' to» means about to, and «tighten belts» means spend less.
fact: In your body, tiny muscles tighten, as when a frightened cat fluffs out its fur or you get goosebumps.
exercise: «Tighten the screw» means? | Loosen it until it falls out | Put it in a box | *Make it firmer, so it holds tight | Paint it red
exercise: «His grip tightened.» What does tightened mean here? | Stopped moving | *Became tighter, squeezing harder | Let go | Slid off
exercise: «The school tightened the rules.» What does tightened mean? | Made the rules longer | Wrote a funny poem about rules | *Made the rules stricter | Removed all the rules
test: Tyrone's mum says, «We fixin' to tighten belts.» What does tighten belts mean? | Buy a new belt | *Spend less money | Dance faster | Wear tighter trousers
test: «When the diaphragm tightens and moves down, the chest gets bigger and air flows into the lungs.» What happens when the diaphragm tightens? | The chest gets smaller and air is pushed out | *The diaphragm moves down and the chest gets bigger | The lungs fall asleep | The diaphragm stops moving completely
exam: Which sentence uses tighten to mean make rules stricter? | «The bike bolt is loose.» | *«We need to tighten up our homework rules.» | «The cat fluffed out its fur.» | «The sun is hot today.»
